  "answer_text": "Here is an overview of **ProFed Credit Union** (accessible at [profedcu.org](https://www.profedcu.org)):\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfe6 About ProFed Credit Union\n\nFounded in 1933, ProFed Credit Union is a **$740 million financial cooperative** with nearly **66,000 member-owners**. They provide financial services to members and businesses all over **Northeast Indiana**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccd Locations & Branches\n\nProFed has **13 branch locations** in Northeast Indiana. Branches are spread across 8 local communities, including **Fort Wayne, Auburn, Decatur, New Haven, and Bluffton**, all within the state of Indiana.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\udd1d Membership Eligibility\n\nYou can own a piece of the credit union with just **$5**. Membership gets you exclusive access to **lower fees and competitive rates**, plus local, personalized service, discounted perks, and a cooperative that supports your community.\n\nYou are eligible to join if you **live, work, worship, attend school, volunteer, or regularly conduct business** in Adams, Allen, DeKalb, Huntington, LaGrange, Noble, Steuben, Wells, and Whitley counties.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Services & Resources\n\nProFed offers a wide range of resources for **kids, adults, and businesses** to help members become empowered on their financial journey \u2014 from budgeting basics to investing and planning for retirement.\n\nThey meet members where they are, offering the ability to **book in-person or virtual meetings** in minutes.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf93 Community Involvement\n\nQualifying students can apply for a **$2,500 ProFed scholarship** to help with college expenses. The company takes pride in its work and community involvement, genuinely caring about employees and sincerely wanting to make a difference for the members they serve.\n\n---\n\n> **Note:** The URL you mentioned \u2014 `www.profedcreditunion.com` \u2014 appears to redirect to their primary website at **[www.profedcu.org](https://www.profedcu.org)**. You can visit that site for full access to account services, loan applications, and more.",
